  "note": "Krita's manual has no single default-shortcut table, so this list is assembled from the pages of the manual that state a default: the Main Menu pages (File, Edit, View, Image, Layer, Select, Help), the Blending Modes page, the Zoom / Freehand Brush / Line / Multibrush / Elliptical Selection / Rectangular Selection / Polygon / Path / Shape Edit / Shape Selection / Text tool pages, the Layers, Advanced Color Selector, Grids and Guides and On-Canvas Brush Editor docker pages, the Adjust filters page, the Canvas Only Mode, Color Selector Settings and General Settings preference pages, the Paint Layers and Vector Layers pages and the Navigation, Snapping, Soft Proofing and \"Introduction to Krita coming from Photoshop\" user-manual pages. The manual documents one set of chords and gives no separate Mac ones, so only `windows` is filled in. The 25 blending-mode chords are the Alt+Shift modifier plus a letter, as the Blending Modes page describes. Left out because the chord grammar cannot express them or because the source is ambiguous: every mouse and stylus binding (all the selection-tool Shift/Alt/Ctrl + click modes, Space + drag panning, Ctrl + Space zooming, Shift + Space rotation, the transform-tool mesh bindings, \"hold R and click\" to pick a layer); the duplicate keys documented for the same command (4 and 6 for canvas rotation alongside Ctrl+[ and Ctrl+], Ctrl+Shift+E under both Flatten Image and \"merges all layers\", Shift+S under both the snap pop-up and grid snapping); \"Next / Previous Blending Mode + and -\", where the page does not say whether the Alt+Shift modifier still applies; Shift+N, which the manual lists as one of \"the two shade selectors\" without saying which; and the Y key on the LUT Management docker, which is not given a command name.",
